---

Competitor Landscape

Competitor: Base

· Category: Ethereum Layer 2 (Optimistic Rollup)
· Difference: Base leads in user volume and transaction activity (~1 million daily active users vs Arbitrum's 250k-300k); processes over 60% of L2 market share; Coinbase-backed retail distribution
· Market Segment: Retail users, high-volume trading

Competitor: Optimism

· Category: Ethereum Layer 2 (Optimistic Rollup)
· Difference: Leads in modular architecture through OP Stack ecosystem (30+ chains including Base, Worldchain, Soneium, Unichain, Kraken's Ink); ~6–8B TVL, 80k-100k daily users
· Market Segment: Modular infrastructure, Superchain ecosystem

Competitor: zkSync Era

· Category: Ethereum Layer 2 (ZK-Rollup)
· Difference: ZK-rollup technology vs Arbitrum's optimistic rollup
· Market Segment: ZK-rollup adoption

Competitor: Starknet

· Category: Ethereum Layer 2 (ZK-Rollup)
· Difference: ZK-rollup with Cairo language
· Market Segment: ZK-rollup development

Catatan: Lebih dari 50 L2 saat ini bersaing untuk pengguna, likuiditas, dan developer; namun pada akhir 2025, pangsa pasar telah terkonsolidasi di sekitar tiga jaringan utama.

